okay hi ian here
basically this won't work properly unless you manually copy the "488final"
folder to downloads and run it from there
vitis should...? cooperate.
if it doesn't make new project, you know the drill. sort xsa's by date.
ALSO. when you update the bitstream, vitis gets... quirky.
you'll need to go to the application project menu, right click it, and in that 
menu, where it says (launch application as debug) you'll need to hover over it
and adjust the debug settings
that launches ANOTHER annoying window, in said annoying window, you need to
go in and enter the "targets" tab and select the new XSA, the new bitstream,
and the init file (click browse, it's the .tcl file that's old as hell)

then click the box that says do post init
if you dont do this, I2C communication wont work and you'll be very sad
